		(uuid "1a70d9ca-c7dc-4e8f-969f-b275f2c027c8")
	)
	(text "The Road Side requires two main voltage levels: 5V (CAN Tranciver) and 3.3V (uC). Because the 5V is available and high efficiency (generated viaa Buck DCDC), \nit is also used for the Relay (it was possibile to also choose it in 3V3 verions).\n\nBecause the 3V3 onlyy supplies light loads, it is acceptable to generate it via LDO (from 5V rail) and not via Buck DCDC. With a negligible power loss in the conversion \nefficincy (in comparison to the powers drawn by realy and motor), there are significant advantages in the costs and ripple of the circuit (important because it \nreduces errors in the ADC readings).\n\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 279.654 107.95 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "27bdb55c-cf12-4d96-8e6a-0391241d3db0")
	)
	(text "Motor output should be mechanically linked \nto a 10kOhm Potentiometer, which is \nconnected to the Board for sensing purposes."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 340.614 87.63 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "29b74d78-dc38-44f3-a348-d7a4b7da75c5")
	)
	(text "\nThe desig of the circuit is the same as Human Side, \npls refer to that schematicto have info about that."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 261.874 251.206 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "32024ae9-7d24-4c8f-8d35-d34afa41a045")
	)
	(text "\"Fault Simulation Connector\", which simlates \nan Open circuit on the Speed sample.\n\nThe pull down is used to guarantee a fixed \nvoltage level even in case of Stuck-Open."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 51.308 38.862 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "349fa0f5-e3aa-497c-a609-c5fd0cfeedf1")
	)
	(text "Motor Interface"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 329.438 45.466 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.4572)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "3c1c0aeb-0784-4f7a-b3f9-975085ecccbc")
	)
	(text "Main Interface"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 352.044 67.056 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.4572)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "3c28b8d8-8bca-43b3-b2d9-cf52745a2ed6")
	)
	(text "\"Fault Simulation Connector\", which simlates \nan Open circuit on the Speed sample.\n\nThe pull down is used to guarantee a fixed \nvoltage level even in case of Stuck-Open."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 52.578 88.392 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "43bf1d3b-7c2f-4a26-ac81-172e4cd37849")
	)
	(text "Similarly to Power Supply, the motor has is owm connector because \nit demands high currents (up to 4.5A spikes).\nThis connector does not need interlock because if it not properly \r\nsecured, the motor will not receive power supply, entering the \r\nfail safe state of motor coasting"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 307.594 59.69 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "44e4a450-588c-4c2f-b97d-3e1656b037b8")
	)
	(text "OK"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 28.702 212.598 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "4c231f4c-f513-4259-b244-ecd7b37f7506")
	)
