	(text "OK"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 28.448 233.934 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "5164ff30-544b-45fe-8596-9e589ec5ec1b")
	)
	(text "Power Supply has its owm connector because \nit has higher current demands (up to 4.5A \nspikes). \nIn order to readuce heating and guaratee \nthe safety during overcurrent situations \n(fuse can blow with currents over 15A, \nin order to be usable at indefinite time \nat 4.5A), the inputs are doubled\nThis connector does not need interlock \nbecause if it not properly  secured, the \nmotor will not receive power supply, \nentering the fail safe state of motor \ncoasting"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 307.594 31.75 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "580586eb-7074-4c6a-ae17-107ef641ab6b")
	)
	(text "From LED datasheet the Typical Voltage drop at 5 mA is 2.95V.\nKnowing this, I can compute the series resistor:\n	R = (3.3V - V_forw_LED) / 5 mA = 70 Ohm\n	--> E12 series (5% Toll.), R = 82 Ohm\n\nIf the Actual Forward Voltage of the LED is higher, it will simply light \nup with lower luminosity, so using the typical Forward Voltage value \nis ok (I don't need to be precise on the actual current flowing in the \nLED, I just need it to light up)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 342.138 228.346 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "5f914a0b-67fd-450a-8a04-89385e576795")
	)
	(text "Connectors"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 352.552 14.732 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.286 2.286)
				(thickness 0.4572)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "619cd2a5-f0d9-44f0-b7ae-5e8b615653e8")
	)
	(text "Connector is doubled to make\nsure it can handle the high \ncurrents in this path"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 358.902 136.906 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "68b084ac-507a-4128-bb32-64b4464b7395")
	)
	(text "The 12V rail input protections are split into 2, because the idea is to split the power supply of \nthe motor and of the electronics that should handle that load. \n(there is only 1 input 12V connector \nfor weight reduction moivations). The protection circuit is completely doubled in order to \nseparate as much as possible for fault containtment porpuses (faults on one side should not\naffect the other one)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 286.258 136.652 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "6b4d4dd4-050f-4ca0-987d-25729523a6ec")
	)
	(text "5V Buck"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 321.564 144.526 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.4572)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "6ff316d3-eb9d-427e-8398-2323150a1f07")
	)
	(text "Power Supply"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 335.788 98.806 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.286 2.286)
				(thickness 0.4572)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "776be629-8a5f-4e5a-8142-85213e4860cf")
	)
	(text "The vehicle speed is simulated using an external, manually controlled 100 kOhm\npotentiometer. Its useful bandwidth is very low, so a first-order RC filter is\nused to reduce wiper noise while keeping the perceived response below 50 ms.\nA maximum settling time of 30 ms is allocated to the analog filter, leaving\nmargin for ADC acquisition and firmware processing.\n\nOpen-Circuit Detection\nA pull-down R_PD of value 100 kOhm defines the ADC input when the wiper connection in the case of a Stuck-Open fault.\nTo distinguish this condition from a valid zero-speed command, the\npotentiometer is connected to GND through a resistor R_G, basically reserving a voltage\nmargin below the normal operating range. \nAs sìdesign constraint, The required minimum valid voltage\nis V_ADC,min >= 0.2 V\n\n    V_TH,min = V_SUPPLY * R_G / (R_POT + R_G)\n    R_TH,min-position = R_POT || R_G\nIn normal conditions, the minimum voltage seen at the Pot. Wiper node is:\n    V_ADC,min = V_TH,min * R_PD / (R_PD + R_F + R_TH,min-position)\n\nWith R_G = 10 kOhm and R_F = 1 kOhm, V_ADC,min = 0.273 V nominal.\nDesign assumptions, to verify against the selected parts and supply:\n    R_POT: +/-20%; fixed resistors: +/-5%; C_F: +/-20%; 3.3 V supply: +/-5%.\nThe lowest voltage occurs with V_SUPPLY,min, R_POT,max, R_G,min, R_F,max\nand R_PD,min. Using these limits gives V_ADC,min = 0.208 V >= 0.2 V.\nAn ADC threshold below 0.2 V (e.g. 0.1 V) can therefore identify an invalid\nlow signal, allowing for ADC errors and noise. This detects a disconnected\nwiper but does not distinguish it from a short to GND.\n\nRC Filter Dimensioning\nThe potentiometer output resistance varies with its position. Including R_G,\nits maximum Thevenin resistance is:\n    R_TH,max = (R_POT + R_G) / 4 = 27.5 kOhm\nThe pull-down also contributes to the resistance seen by the capacitor:\n    R_EQ,max = (R_TH,max + R_F) || R_PD = 22.18 kOhm\n    tau_max = R_EQ,max * C_F; T_settle ~= 5 * tau_max\n\nSelecting C_F = C1 = 150 nF gives T_settle,max = 16.6 ms nominal.\nUsing maximum resistances and capacitance gives:\n    R_TH,max,worst = (120k + 10.5k) / 4 = 32.625 kOhm\n    R_EQ,max,worst = (32.625k + 1.05k) || 105k = 25.50 kOhm\n    T_settle,max,worst = 5 * 25.50k * 180n = 22.95 ms < 30 ms.\n\nWhen the wiper is disconnected, C_F discharges through R_PD only:\n    tau_OC = R_PD * C_F = 15 ms nominal\n    T_settle,OC,worst = 5 * 105k * 180n = 94.5 ms.\nFault recognition must allow for this discharge transient; the 30 ms target\napplies to normal operation, not to an open-circuit event.\n\nR_PD loads the potentiometer, making the voltage-position relationship\nnonlinear. The firmware mapping must account for this loading and the offset\nintroduced by R_G. Noise rejection and response time will be checked on bench."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 140.97 24.13 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
			(href "#1")
		)
		(uuid "77da6792-d0e5-4afa-b04e-c0e295856906")
	)
	(text "Interlock End"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 375.92 75.184 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "7a02d7df-69e9-412c-9b19-429567ca89ee")
	)
	(text "The bus uses split termination with two 60.4 Ohm resistors and a 4.7nF capacitor \nconnected from their midpoint to GND. The two resistors provide approximately \n120 Ohm differential termination, while the capacitor creates a low-pass filtering\neffect for common-mode noise. \nDuring normal CAN communication, CANH and CANL move in opposite directions, so the \nmidpoint voltage remains approximately constant and the capacitor has\nlittle effect on the differential signal.\r\n\nA larger capacitor would provide stronger common-mode filtering, but could also \nintroduce problems under the fault situation when when one CAN line becomes \ndisconnected. In this case, the differential symmetry is lost and the capacitor \ncan affect the useful signal, introducing an RC delay that may prevent the signal \nfrom reaching the required voltage thresholds before the CAN sampling point. \nFor this reason, 4.7nF was selected instead of a much larger value, such as \n100nF, to obtain some common-mode filtering without unnecessarily \ndegrading signal integrity under fault conditions.\r\n\r\nThe termination resistors are sized considering possible short circuit fault to \nthe 12V main supply of one of the CAN lines, which should not result in fathal \nmalfunctions.\n	P_MAX = (12V / (2*60.4))^2 * 60.4 = 0.596 W \n	--> Max power loss on each resitor\n	-->	Termination resistor should at least be rated for 1 W (and PCB should\n		be designed to handle the heat dissipation)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 246.38 34.29 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "7d499f8d-f462-4eba-9a09-beaf7c21790e")
	)
	(text "CAN"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 246.888 15.494 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.286 2.286)
				(thickness 0.4572)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "81844af8-c1a0-4382-9786-15700af297fd")
	)
	(text "No common-mode choke is used, since no dedicated EMC testing is\nplanned to calibrate its parameters, guaranteeing an actual \nimprovement of the CAN performance."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 201.422 23.622 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "82bb3d17-0cf0-47f0-8cd3-79c2a83ac905")
	)
	(text "Power Supply Interface"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 329.184 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.4572)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "8382b6cd-631d-47a2-bc08-e5748d021ade")
	)
	(text "OK"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 28.448 210.058 0)
		(effects
			(font
