	(text "3V3 LDO"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 323.342 198.12 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.4572)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "e92d291f-e885-4506-80cb-e355aab75f2c")
	)
	(text "nRST circuit generates a signal that is normally \nHIGH (no reset), and LOW when button is pressed \n(reset). the capacitor is used to filter this \nsignal, and in particular avoid noise and EMI to \ntrigger the reset condition."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 187.198 244.856 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "f3463c1c-8796-4cb6-9404-7d42aafadc26")
	)
	(text "TVS diode is used to improve the ESD strike resistance of the \nCAN tranciver. It allows to withstand automotive standard ISO \n10605 30kV stikes, in comparison to the 8kV strikes for which \nthe CAN tranciver is rated. \n\nTVS diode must be placed as close as possible the CAN connector \ntoprotect efficiently the CAN transceiver. A direct connection \nto wide GND plane is required to disspate efficiently energy \nfrom the ESD strike with a low impedance return path. \n\nThe TVS is bidirectional to proect against ESD strikes with both \npolarities. It has a 24V working voltage (V_RWM) to avoid \nconducting during normal operations and during possible \nsustained overvoltage conditions (1 CAN line is shorted to 12V \nMain Supply). \nThe clamping voltage (V_CL), the voltage reached during a strike \nis 33V, which is less than the maximum absolute rating of the \ntranciver CAN pins of 42V, ensuring that the strike won't \nactually damage the tranciver.\nThe capacitance of 31pF added on each CAN line is small, \nbasically not degrading the dynamic perfomance of the CAN.\n\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 234.442 84.836 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "f40e3162-479f-480c-9094-c29baf8583ac")
	)
	(text "Only the Motor 12V is checked in order to make sure that \nthe the Conntrol ELectronics can recognise and properly \nhandl situations in which the Motor can not actually\nbe controller (because it has no power supply)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 262.128 257.048 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "f94414e9-d1dd-4559-8fef-339fa952fb5b")
	)
	(text "The Inductor proposed by the TI design was not available, so a new one, \ncompatible with the DCDC circuit requirements is selected using the \nfollowing constraints\n\n    - DC resistance: <= 450 mOhm (to maintain or improve the DCDC efficiency)\n    - Saturation Current: From the report, the max current on L is 379.036 mA\n        --> I_SAT >= 0.6 A (to guarantee some margin)\n    - RMS Current: Considering the current on L as a triangular wave (it is \n		a simplification), the RMS current is computed as:\n        --> I_RMS = sqrt(I_OUT^2 + (Delta_I_L^2 / 12)) \n				= sqrt(0.25^2 + (0.25807^2 / 12)) = 0.261 A\n        --> I_RMS >= 0.5 A (to have some margin)\n\n    - L should be preferably shielded to reduce EMI emissions"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 250.444 178.308 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "fb91e79e-74f2-4b9d-841d-76e0f66067c5")
	)
	(text "VTRef"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 361.442 42.418 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "ff4b9ed8-9979-4539-a6e0-cc22bda25a4a")
